WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:03.234
-Welcome back to "Late Night".
We're here with Jonathan Majors.

00:00:03.234 --> 00:00:05.834
Now you obviously have some
athletic experience.

00:00:05.834 --> 00:00:07.434
I know you grew up in Texas,
you played basketball,

00:00:07.434 --> 00:00:08.501
you played football.

00:00:08.501 --> 00:00:12.734
But you also were a poet
at a young age.

00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:16.400
-I was a poet at a young age.
-Yeah, and you had a poet name.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.400
-Yes, the advent
of J. Manifesto.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.601
-J. Manifesto.
-Yes.

00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:23.567
-That is a very good poet name.

00:00:23.567 --> 00:00:24.734
-Thank you.
-Especially for

00:00:24.734 --> 00:00:26.467
Jonathan Majors, I think
that's a really good one.

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:28.567
-Same initials.
-Yep.

00:00:28.567 --> 00:00:30.534
-I had it put on the back
of my letterman jacket.

00:00:30.534 --> 00:00:32.801
-Wow.
-Yeah, it said "Manifesto".

00:00:32.801 --> 00:00:34.234
I thought it was very artsy
and cool.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.534
-Yeah, that's a real nice
combination of, like,

00:00:36.534 --> 00:00:38.000
sports and arts.
-Jock.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.567
-Yeah, a letterman jacket with
your poetry name on the back.

00:00:40.567 --> 00:00:44.467
-There was the football.

00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:48.100
There was my number
and then the mask.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.100
-Oh, really? You had the, like,
the comedy and drama masks?

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.434
-Yeah, I had all the patches.
-That's great.

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:52.868
-And then it had "J. Manifesto"
on the back --

00:00:52.868 --> 00:00:54.400
no, it had "Manifesto"
on the back.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:57.234
-Yeah.
-And then I was expelled

00:00:57.234 --> 00:00:58.767
two days after I got it.
-Really?

00:00:58.767 --> 00:00:59.968
-Yeah.

00:00:59.968 --> 00:01:02.100
-What were you expelled for?
-Psh! Everything.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.300
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:04.634
-Oh, they got you on everything
all at once?

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:06.334
-I was at Rico.
-[ Laughs ] Rico.

00:01:06.334 --> 00:01:07.501
-Rico, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:10.901
I gave it to my first love
who still has it.

00:01:10.901 --> 00:01:12.267
-Really?
-Yeah, it's in a closet

00:01:12.267 --> 00:01:13.968
someplace.
-That's -- oh, yeah, wow.

00:01:13.968 --> 00:01:15.734
-Yeah, if I could get that back,
that'd be...

00:01:15.734 --> 00:01:17.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.634 --> 00:01:22.234
-Yeah, first loves tend to check
out interviews with their,

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:24.167
you know, former amours.
-I reckon.

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:26.367
-Yeah.

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:27.534
You spent some --

00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:29.334
You worked at --
before you were an actor

00:01:29.334 --> 00:01:31.567
and, I guess,
after you were a poet --

00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:34.467
you worked at a number of chains
we're familiar with.

00:01:34.467 --> 00:01:36.434
Olive Garden, Starbucks,
Party City.

00:01:36.434 --> 00:01:37.634
-Olive Garden, Starbucks,
Party City.

00:01:37.634 --> 00:01:40.334
-Red Lobster.
-Red Lobster, Quiznos Subs...

00:01:40.334 --> 00:01:44.000
-Wow.
-...Braum's Ice Creamery...

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.033
-Okay.
-No, you don't know Braum's.

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:48.334
[ Laughter ]
You don't know Braum's.

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:50.567
-I will say it was said
like they knew.

00:01:50.567 --> 00:01:51.801
-It was. I was like, "What?"

00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:53.634
-It wasn't like one
of those loose "whoos".

00:01:53.634 --> 00:01:54.767
It was like, "Yeah."

00:01:54.767 --> 00:01:56.033
-Yeah, "Can I get the double
with the --"

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:58.067
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Yeah, it was great, man.

00:01:58.067 --> 00:02:00.734
Like, working
at a Halloween shop was cool.

00:02:00.734 --> 00:02:03.100
You'd see costumes, you'd go,
"Oh, nice, interesting.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:06.167
This person is playing Velma
from 'Scooby-Doo'."

00:02:06.167 --> 00:02:07.901
And you're just thinking about
what that person's like,

00:02:07.901 --> 00:02:09.200
you know, and you were like,
"Nice."

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.100
And then you work at Quiznos,
and all of a sudden,

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:13.601
you know, you're
an Italian sandwich man.

00:02:13.601 --> 00:02:14.901
-Yeah.

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.868
-And carbonera, you know, you
really invest in --

00:02:16.868 --> 00:02:18.300
[Italian accent] "Carbonera,"
[Normal voice] you know?

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.901
-So these were, in a way, you
were just taking them on as

00:02:20.901 --> 00:02:22.701
roles before your bigger roles.

00:02:22.701 --> 00:02:23.968
-Bro, I had to.
-Yeah.

00:02:23.968 --> 00:02:26.601
-I was working maybe two
or three of them at a time.

00:02:26.601 --> 00:02:27.868
-Gotcha.
-And still trying to do

00:02:27.868 --> 00:02:29.934
the whole letterman thing.
-And then you were in

00:02:29.934 --> 00:02:31.868
New York City for a brief
period of time, right?

00:02:31.868 --> 00:02:33.501
-Then I went to North Carolina
School of the Arts,

00:02:33.501 --> 00:02:35.234
another school.
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:02:35.234 --> 00:02:37.267
-There you go, they knew it.
-Guys.

00:02:37.267 --> 00:02:39.033
Yeah, she knew it.
-Pickles!

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:40.367
-Pickles? Okay, you're in.

00:02:40.367 --> 00:02:42.133
You're in, you're in, you're in.

00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:45.934
Yeah, and I worked here
in New York City.

00:02:45.934 --> 00:02:49.367
I was following around a mentor
named Ruben Santiago-Hudson.

00:02:49.367 --> 00:02:51.734
-Mm-hmm.
-And was trying to get

00:02:51.734 --> 00:02:53.400
in his rehearsal room
as much as possible.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.467
But I was also working
on Second Avenue,

00:02:55.467 --> 00:02:57.200
and there was three bars
on Second Avenue --

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.334
two of them
which are still there --

00:02:59.334 --> 00:03:00.667
and I worked at them.

00:03:00.667 --> 00:03:04.534
I was the -- I played the role
of the bar-back...

00:03:04.534 --> 00:03:05.834
-Uh-huh.
-...the host...

00:03:05.834 --> 00:03:09.300
-Yeah.
-...the bouncer...

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:10.501
-So you could do it all?
-...the runner.

00:03:10.501 --> 00:03:12.033
-Yeah.
-I mean, yeah, I was --

00:03:12.033 --> 00:03:14.501
-When you came in wearing
that poetry-and-football jacket,

00:03:14.501 --> 00:03:16.567
they were like, "I think he can
handle almost anything."

00:03:16.567 --> 00:03:18.167
-Yeah, I could do everything.

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:21.000
-Do people -- especially, you
know, obviously, New York City,

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.634
you work in bars,
colorful characters,

00:03:22.634 --> 00:03:24.100
but they're also
your colleagues --

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:25.467
do you hear from those people
still?

00:03:25.467 --> 00:03:27.767
Are they proud of where
this has all ended up for you?

00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:29.467
-Well, full circle, bro.

00:03:29.467 --> 00:03:31.434
'Cause we chatted right before
I went to "SNL".

00:03:31.434 --> 00:03:33.000
-That's right. We talked
right beforehand.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.400
You were fantastic.
-Thank you.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:37.434
-You're very welcome.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:37.434 --> 00:03:40.601
-When I hit "SNL",
they blew me up.

00:03:40.601 --> 00:03:42.634
For whatever reason, "SNL"
and those bars --

00:03:42.634 --> 00:03:45.067
they were just like, "Oh,
my God, Jonathan, we knew.

00:03:45.067 --> 00:03:46.234
This and that. Blah, blah, blah,
blah, blah, blah,

00:03:46.234 --> 00:03:47.267
blah, blah, blah."
Now it's like,

00:03:47.267 --> 00:03:48.367
"Oh, love you guys."
-Yeah.

00:03:48.367 --> 00:03:49.667
-So, yeah, like, we stay tight.

00:03:49.667 --> 00:03:51.868
-That's wonderful.
-Yeah, these movies go up,

00:03:51.868 --> 00:03:55.067
and I get pictures of Kang,
you know.

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:57.033
They send it to me, and I go,
"All love, man."

00:03:57.033 --> 00:03:58.434
-Yeah, that's fantastic.

00:03:58.434 --> 00:04:00.367
Well, no one ever expects when
they're, you know, working

00:04:00.367 --> 00:04:02.234
with a bar-back, that one day
they're gonna be Kang.

00:04:02.234 --> 00:04:03.701
You know, that's...
-True! True, true.

00:04:03.701 --> 00:04:05.767
-That's true. They might think
you're gonna host "SNL",

00:04:05.767 --> 00:04:06.801
but at the time --
-Kang.

00:04:06.801 --> 00:04:07.901
-I think it's gonna be Kang.

00:04:07.901 --> 00:04:09.133
-No, nobody thought that.

00:04:09.133 --> 00:04:11.234
Nobody thought that.
-Now you have a 9-year-old

00:04:11.234 --> 00:04:12.400
daughter.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:14.033
Is there any of your work
that she's engaged with?

00:04:14.033 --> 00:04:15.067
Is she impressed with her dad?

00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:17.701
Or is this stuff a little...

00:04:17.701 --> 00:04:19.734
-She's impressed when I throw
her very high...

00:04:19.734 --> 00:04:21.667
-Oh, that's good.
-...and she lands on the bed.

00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:23.400
-All right.
-Right now, she's having

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:24.767
a bit of a moment.
-Okay.

00:04:24.767 --> 00:04:27.133
-My daughter's 9, almost 10.
-Okay.

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:30.634
-And recently [Sighs]
much to my chagrin,

00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:33.133
young boys are walking up to her
and saying,

00:04:33.133 --> 00:04:36.367
"You know, you look a lot
like Kang."

00:04:36.367 --> 00:04:37.801
-Oh, wow.

00:04:37.801 --> 00:04:40.701
-And my daughter looks at them
and goes, "That's my daddy."

00:04:40.701 --> 00:04:49.267
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.267 --> 00:04:53.067
So she's dealing with that,
and, I mean, she was starstruck

00:04:53.067 --> 00:04:55.701
by Paul Rudd.
-Yeah, well, who isn't?

00:04:55.701 --> 00:04:57.000
-Fair point.
-Yeah, I mean,

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:59.667
all ages, all walks of life.

00:04:59.667 --> 00:05:01.467
-Fair point, fair point,
fair point.

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:03.701
-Well, she has a lot to be
impressed about.

00:05:03.701 --> 00:05:05.000
It is always so wonderful
to see you.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:06.267
Thanks so much for being here.

00:05:06.267 --> 00:05:07.434
-This is worth it, man.

00:05:07.434 --> 00:05:09.067
Thank you.
-Congratulations on your films.

00:05:09.067 --> 00:05:10.734
Congratulate Jonathan Majors.

00:05:10.734 --> 00:05:13.334
"Creed III" in theaters
and IMAX tomorrow.

00:05:13.334 --> 00:05:15.701
And "Ant-Man and the Wasp:
Quantumania" also out now.

00:05:15.701 --> 00:05:17.300
Be right back with Riley Keough.

